RESULT

The classification algorithms ID3, J48, Naïve Bayes, and k-Nearest Neighbour were studied using the WEKA Machine Learning Toolkit. The Iris dataset was loaded and examined through the Preprocess panel, and discretization was performed to understand the transformation of numeric attributes into nominal intervals.

The J48 algorithm was used to construct and visualize a decision tree, while Naïve Bayes and IBk were examined for classification. The concepts of entropy, information gain, and the Kappa statistic were studied. Classification rules were extracted from the decision tree, and ROC curves were examined using the threshold-curve visualization feature.

Thus, the experiment demonstrated the application and evaluation of different classification algorithms in WEKA. The performance of each classifier can be compared using the actual accuracy, Kappa statistic, confusion matrix, and ROC/AUC results obtained during execution.
